  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Job",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 16,
    "summary": "Job speaks against the wicked who oppose him—Though even his friends scorn him, he testifies that his witness is in heaven and his record is on high.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Then Job answered and said,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 16:1",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "I have heard many such things: miserable comforters are ye all.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "Job 13:4; D&C 121:10 (7–11)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 55
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 16:2",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Shall vain words have an end? or what emboldeneth thee that thou answerest?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 16:3",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "I also could speak as ye do: if your soul were in my soul’s stead, I could heap up words against you, and shake mine head at you.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 28
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 16:4",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "But I would strengthen you with my mouth, and the moving of my lips should assuage your grief.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3
          },
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 94
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 16:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Though I speak, my grief is not assuaged: and though I forbear, what am I eased?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 52
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 16:6",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "But now he hath made me weary: thou hast made desolate all my company.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 16:7",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And thou hast filled me with wrinkles, which is a witness against me: and my leanness rising up in me beareth witness to my face.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 44
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 69
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 16:8",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "He teareth me in his wrath, who hateth me: he gnasheth upon me with his teeth; mine enemy sharpeneth his eyes upon me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 13
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 16:9",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "They have gaped upon me with their mouth; they have smitten me upon the cheek reproachfully; they have gathered themselves together against me.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 91,
            "text": "TG Reproach."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Reproach.",
            "prettyString": "TG Reproach",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Reproach",
                "entryId": "tg-reproach",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 16:10",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "God hath delivered me to the ungodly, and turned me over into the hands of the wicked.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 16:11",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "I was at ease, but he hath broken me asunder: he hath also taken me by my neck, and shaken me to pieces, and set me up for his mark.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 16:12",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "His archers compass me round about, he cleaveth my reins asunder, and doth not spare; he poureth out my gall upon the ground.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 16:13",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "He breaketh me with breach upon breach, he runneth upon me like a giant.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "HEB mighty man."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 16:14",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "I have sewed sackcloth upon my skin, and defiled my horn in the dust.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "OR cast my strength."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 16:15",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "My face is foul with weeping, and on my eyelids is the shadow of death;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 50
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 16:16",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "Not for any injustice in mine hands: also my prayer is pure.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 11
          },
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 54
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 16:17",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "O earth, cover not thou my blood, and let my cry have no place.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 16:18",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "Also now, behold, my witness is in heaven, and my record is on high.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "TG Heaven."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 31
          },
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Heaven.",
            "prettyString": "TG Heaven",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
